- He always eats well.

89
00:03:44,800 --> 00:03:45,930
Oh, my.

90
00:03:48,030 --> 00:03:49,330
- Do you know each other?
- This is the first time...

91
00:03:49,430 --> 00:03:50,540
- We're meeting for the first time.
- We're meeting for the first time.

92
00:03:50,640 --> 00:03:52,170
- He's shy.
- Really?

93
00:03:52,170 --> 00:03:54,210
- I've seen him a lot in videos.
- Right.

94
00:03:54,210 --> 00:03:55,970
- Me too.
- Why do you keep looking at me?

95
00:03:56,270 --> 00:03:57,740
He's shy.

96
00:03:57,740 --> 00:03:59,840
- Because he's...
- I'm sure you'll gradually...

97
00:03:59,840 --> 00:04:01,780
- He's a veteran actor.
- Are you shy too?

98
00:04:01,910 --> 00:04:03,310
Well... Yes.

99
00:04:06,220 --> 00:04:08,090
- We've worked together before.
- On what?

100
00:04:08,350 --> 00:04:09,520
- What?
- Wait.

101
00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:11,060
- Guess.
- Make a guess.

102
00:04:11,160 --> 00:04:12,260
It was a commercial.

103
00:04:12,420 --> 00:04:13,760
- A commercial?
- Come on.

104
00:04:13,760 --> 00:04:15,860
But it'll be hard to remember. It was a long time ago.

105
00:04:16,030 --> 00:04:17,660
I think 2010?

106
00:04:18,330 --> 00:04:20,930
(He doesn't remember it at all.)

107
00:04:22,100 --> 00:04:23,970
He has absolutely no idea.

108
00:04:24,070 --> 00:04:25,570
- Wait! I remembered!
- What?

109
00:04:25,570 --> 00:04:27,210
- I remembered. A beer commercial.
- What was it?

110
00:04:27,340 --> 00:04:29,110
- Right?
- Oh, my.

111
00:04:29,110 --> 00:04:31,840
- A beer commercial. Right?
- Oh, my.

112
00:04:31,840 --> 00:04:33,310
- You're right.
- Really?

113
00:04:33,310 --> 00:04:35,510
- It was a comedic one.
- It was.

114
00:04:35,510 --> 00:04:38,450
That was 16 years ago.

115
00:04:38,450 --> 00:04:39,750
It was 16 years ago.

116
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:41,020
- Right.
- Oh, my.

117
00:04:41,020 --> 00:04:42,890
- Let's speak casually.
- Let's both speak casually.

118
00:04:42,890 --> 00:04:44,460
- You too.
- I'll speak casually to you too.

119
00:04:44,460 --> 00:04:47,060
- Please do.
- Since you're both older than me...

120
00:04:47,130 --> 00:04:48,830
No, don't be so formal.

121
00:04:48,930 --> 00:04:50,300
Don't be like that. It makes us feel old.

122
00:04:50,300 --> 00:04:52,130
- Just treat us like older brothers.
- Okay.

123
00:04:52,130 --> 00:04:53,230
Brothers.

124
00:04:53,230 --> 00:04:55,830
(Just like that on the water, they became three brothers.)

125
00:04:56,200 --> 00:04:57,900
- Hyun Moo. It keeps...
- What?

126
00:04:58,070 --> 00:04:59,700
- What is that?
- That's so cool.

127
00:04:59,800 --> 00:05:02,040
- Is that nature?
- A whirlpool.

128
00:05:02,040 --> 00:05:03,240
Uzushio.

129
00:05:03,980 --> 00:05:05,580
- Is this okay?
- You're right. Oh, my.

130
00:05:05,740 --> 00:05:08,510
- Look at that.
- Like "Pirates of the Caribbean."

131
00:05:08,780 --> 00:05:10,480
- It looks like CGI.
- Seriously, with that boat...

132
00:05:12,350 --> 00:05:14,420
This is Naruto Strait.

133
00:05:14,420 --> 00:05:15,450
(Naruto Strait)

134
00:05:15,520 --> 00:05:16,990
There's something called The World's Top Three Currents.

135
00:05:17,420 --> 00:05:19,290
One is in Italy, and one is in Canada.

136
00:05:20,260 --> 00:05:21,430
And then this one here.

137
00:05:22,090 --> 00:05:24,160
So this is the Seto Inland Sea.

138
00:05:24,360 --> 00:05:27,430
It's a sea that's connected to the Pacific Ocean.

139
00:05:28,030 --> 00:05:29,430
So there's a difference in water levels.

140
00:05:29,430 --> 00:05:30,600
(The difference in tide levels creates this whirlpool.)

141
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:32,570
At the fastest points,

142
00:05:32,570 --> 00:05:34,110
the current speed is over 20km per hour.

143
00:05:34,870 --> 00:05:36,340
Oh, that's really fast.

144
00:05:36,340 --> 00:05:37,780
That's why the seafood here is good.

145
00:05:38,180 --> 00:05:39,610
So in here, there are...

146
00:05:39,840 --> 00:05:41,150
- Yes, there are.
- I see.

147
00:05:41,150 --> 00:05:43,350
- Since the current is strong, - Yes.

148
00:05:43,610 --> 00:05:46,080
the sea bream that can swim against it are famous.

149
00:05:46,850 --> 00:05:48,520
The flesh, I've tried it before,

150
00:05:48,520 --> 00:05:49,820
- is so nice and chewy.
- It must be so chewy.

151
00:05:50,020 --> 00:05:51,620
So can we eat sea bream today?

152
00:05:51,860 --> 00:05:53,660
What else would three guys do besides eating?

153
00:05:54,360 --> 00:05:55,630
- Let's go. I'm hungry.
- Let's go.

154
00:05:55,630 --> 00:05:56,730
Let's go.

155
00:05:57,030 --> 00:05:58,330
Where do we go? Do we go on this?

156
00:06:00,800 --> 00:06:03,000
(Naruto Port)

157
00:06:03,370 --> 00:06:05,340
What's our mode of transport?

158
00:06:05,640 --> 00:06:06,770
I rented something.

159
00:06:07,040 --> 00:06:08,170
You already did?

160
00:06:08,710 --> 00:06:09,970
Oh, really? Where?

161
00:06:10,210 --> 00:06:11,240
- I got it.
- I...

162
00:06:11,240 --> 00:06:12,880
I brought my international driver's license.

163
00:06:12,880 --> 00:06:14,880
- I did too.
- Just in case... Here.

164
00:06:16,050 --> 00:06:17,180
- Here.
- You can drive.

165
00:06:17,580 --> 00:06:19,650
- Have you driven here before?
- That's a nice picture.

166
00:06:19,980 --> 00:06:21,620
- It really is.
- It's like a baby picture.

167
00:06:21,820 --> 00:06:23,150
Your eyes are so bright.

168
00:06:23,150 --> 00:06:24,420
(Bright eyes)

169
00:06:25,460 --> 00:06:26,920
Isn't this a mugshot?

170
00:06:26,920 --> 00:06:29,360
I took this in a rush.

171
00:06:29,360 --> 00:06:30,600
It looks like a baby picture.

172
00:06:30,960 --> 00:06:32,130
Right.

173
00:06:32,130 --> 00:06:34,600
(Glaring)

174
00:06:34,870 --> 00:06:37,000
- Don't I look scary?
- It's like from "The Outlaws."

175
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:38,140
Right? Aren't I scary?

176
00:06:38,240 --> 00:06:40,370
The first guy that dies in "The Outlaws."

177
00:06:40,910 --> 00:06:41,970
That kind of face.

178
00:06:42,240 --> 00:06:44,680
- You don't drive, right?
- Of course, I do.

179
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:47,040
- I like driving.
- I like driving overseas.

180
00:06:47,150 --> 00:06:48,510
- I see.
- So I always rent a car.

181
00:06:48,950 --> 00:06:50,080
So should...

182
00:06:50,450 --> 00:06:51,750
You said you hadn't driven on the right side before.

183
00:06:51,750 --> 00:06:54,790
It's all the same. If someone asks, "What are you best at in life?"

184
00:06:54,790 --> 00:06:56,390
I'd say driving.

185
00:06:57,160 --> 00:06:58,320
That's me.

186
00:06:58,320 --> 00:07:00,530
- I'm similar to you.
- You two decide and let me know.

187
00:07:00,530 --> 00:07:01,830
Where's the car?

188
00:07:02,130 --> 00:07:03,930
Which car is it? I'll ride in the back.

189
00:07:05,130 --> 00:07:06,400
I rented a big car.

190
00:07:06,660 --> 00:07:07,770
It's an SUV.

191
00:07:09,570 --> 00:07:11,270
I'll drive first.

192
00:07:11,270 --> 00:07:12,270
Since you haven't driven...

193
00:07:12,270 --> 00:07:13,270
- on the right side.
- Okay.

194
00:07:13,270 --> 00:07:14,640
See if it seems doable.

195
00:07:16,870 --> 00:07:18,810
- Oh, my.
- Oh, it's hot.

196
00:07:19,810 --> 00:07:21,750
It does feel weird to have the wheel on the right.

197
00:07:21,880 --> 00:07:22,980
Joon, look.

198
00:07:23,150 --> 00:07:24,280
Which way do we go from here?

199
00:07:24,280 --> 00:07:25,980
- To the left or to the right?
- To the left, of course.

200
00:07:27,120 --> 00:07:30,050
- Of course. My talent is...
- Driving on the right is confusing.

201
00:07:30,050 --> 00:07:31,160
Come on.

202
00:07:31,420 --> 00:07:33,420
Look. It feels like you're driving the wrong direction.

203
00:07:33,420 --> 00:07:34,660
At first, it feels very weird.

204
00:07:34,660 --> 00:07:35,690
(Korea and Japan have driving lanes on opposite sides.)

205
00:07:45,240 --> 00:07:47,240
- Oh, my.
- Oh, my.

206
00:07:47,810 --> 00:07:49,670
- Oh, my. What is this place?
- They must fish a lot here.

207
00:07:53,110 --> 00:07:56,910
(Drive down the road, following the scent of the ocean,)

208
00:07:58,580 --> 00:08:01,450
(and travellers are greeted with green fields.)

209
00:08:02,350 --> 00:08:04,220
They kept the old houses just as they were.

210
00:08:04,220 --> 00:08:05,260
